 "name": "rod_control_cell",
 "description": "11x21 INSL-jacketed per-rod control cell: two WIFI inputs (up/down) over NSCN, a 5-wide SWCH button row with PSCN/NSCN taps, and one WIFI output. Three of these side by side = the source's manual rod bank.",
 "why": "Save 2001108 tiles this cell 3x at x=45,57,69 (y=30-50) and again at y=54-74. Each cell listens on two channels (11 and 13 for cell 1), a spark on the SWCH row (x=50-54,y=39) latches it, and the output WIFI (bottom, ch 3/5/7 per cell) drives that rod's PSTN. Deviation: empty cells beside the WIFI cells filled with INSL (lint); the NSCN/PSCN taps that must touch each WIFI are kept as captured, so one open face per WIFI remains and lint still flags it -- required for the circuit to work.",
 "source": "save 2001108, x45-55 y30-50 (cell 1); WIFI (50,31) ch11, (54,31) ch13, (48,44) ch45, (50,49) ch3",
